        {
          "id": 1941891181,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I internalised this comment (written by @guyharris) in check_tfs.py:\n\n            # Do not do this check for plugins; plugins cannot import\n            # data values from libwireshark (functions, yes; data\n            # values, no).\n\nAssuming this is right, plugins (internal or external) cannot share them anyway.  It is possible that externally-maintained built-in dissectors reference the ones I deleted, but they would hardly be common..\n\nI don't feel strongly about deleting them - 2 are common words where the order wouldn't likely be reversed, the other one was quite specialised and only appears in one order.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-09T09:01:43.351Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-12T16:49:07.903Z",
